This thesis marks the conclusion of an important phase of my studies and reflects the knowledge, experience and insights I have gained throughout my practical training at Hitachi Energy.

I would like to express my sincere gratitude to my supervisor, Marco Van-Rosmalen, whose guidance, support and expertise were invaluable throughout this project. His willingness to share knowledge, provide constructive feedback and encourage independent thinking significantly contributed to both the quality of this work and my professional development.

I am also deeply thankful to the entire team in Rotterdam. Their openness, technical expertise and readiness to help created an inspiring and supportive working environment in which I was able to grow both personally and professionally. The many discussions, shared experiences and collaborative efforts made this project not only a valuable learning opportunity but also an enjoyable journey.

Beyond the technical aspects of the project, my time in Rotterdam was an unforgettable experience. I was fortunate to work alongside talented and welcoming colleagues who made me feel part of the team from the very beginning. The friendly atmosphere, mutual support and memorable moments I shared with the team made my stay particularly rewarding and contributed greatly to my overall experience.

Finally, I would like to thank everyone who supported me during my studies and throughout the completion of this thesis. Their encouragement and belief in my abilities have been greatly appreciated.
